Again, it's always taking

464
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:20,460
the whole picture into
account, talking to your

465
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:23,500
patients, history and
physical, putting it together.

466
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:27,830
And number three, how do
you diagnose anaphylaxis?

467
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:30,400
Hypotension within
minutes to hours

468
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:33,200
after exposure to
a known allergen.

469
00:24:34,210 --> 00:24:36,540
And in all honesty, when
we look back and think

470
00:24:36,540 --> 00:24:38,200
about this patient that
I just told you the

471
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:40,540
story of the naproxen
guy, he actually met the

472
00:24:40,540 --> 00:24:42,800
criteria of anaphylaxis
by number three, except

473
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:44,880
he didn't know it was
an allergen at the time.

474
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:48,020
He learned later that it
was an allergen after his

475
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:50,940
